<title>SWEDEN: Iceland airport moves 34 pct more cargo in Oct.</title>
<headline>Iceland airport moves 34 pct more cargo in Oct.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Iceland's international airport at Keflavik handled 34 percent more freight in October, Iceland's civil aviation administration said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The administration published the following figures about airport activity for the month.</p>
<p>				   Oct 1996 Oct 1995</p>
<p>KEFLAVIK INT'L AIRPORT</p>
<p> Cargo export (in tonnes)     1,366		     934</p>
<p>	 import			 602		     531</p>
<p>	 Total			1,968		   1,465</p>
<p> Mail  export (in tonnes)	  59			46</p>
<p>	 import			 135		     134</p>
<p>	 Total			  194		     180</p>
<p> Passengers			91,861		  75,745</p>
<p>-- Abigail Schmelz, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1003</p>
</text>
